# qwen3.5-agent:9b - tuned for AGENTIC / tool-driving work, not pure codegen.
#
# The problem this fixes: paragraph-scale "semantic loops" where the model
# re-derives the same reasoning over and over in its thinking block.
#
# Why the code-tuned variant loops:
#   * repeat_last_n defaults to 64 tokens. A paragraph loop cycles over ~150+
#     tokens, so it is OUTSIDE the penalty window - the sampler cannot see it.
#   * presence_penalty 0 (correct for code, so identifiers can repeat) removes
#     the only long-range brake.
#   * temperature 0.3 makes sampling near-deterministic, so once a cycle starts
#     the same tokens keep winning and there is no escape velocity.
#
# Fixes, in order of importance:
FROM huihui_ai/qwen3.5-abliterated:9b

# Window widened past paragraph scale so repeat_penalty can actually SEE the loop
PARAMETER repeat_last_n 1024
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

# Mild long-range brake. Deliberately NOT 1.5 - that would harm code by
# penalising reused identifiers. 0.4 discourages re-derivation without that cost.
PARAMETER presence_penalty 0.4

# Qwen3.5's own recommended thinking-mode temperature. Enough entropy to break
# out of a cycle; still low enough to be faithful when editing code.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER min_p 0
